  "algorithm_additions": [
    "v10 is a separate v7/v8/v9 lineage, not our v0.8.2 fixed-lane/interleaved-memory search.",
    "Bounded tensor/consumer gathering and writer-closed splitting; candidates ranked by distinct-core marginal traffic, pipeline load and overlapping lifetime pressure.",
    "Three directions share 48 cheap move evaluations; retain two per direction; refine up to eight candidates, and share 48 replay/12 refinement work across up to three feedback starts.",
    "Final shortlist retains the original three candidates, expands to six, then adds up to four timeline and four spill-order candidates from a fixed seed; max fourteen whole-plan exact timing evaluations.",
    "Exact final ranking allows traffic increases if cycles decrease; ties use total traffic. Reported exact stage implements official Step2/Step3/Scene B and CPython set ordering.",
    "Binary-search spill incarnation lookup replaces a prefix scan in the transplanted official spill model; it does not apply to our independent solver path."
  ],
